      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Self-managing medication risks based on online forums is very dangerous, regardless of the dose size. Increasing your dose of Sertraline when you feel jittery is not a safe or appropriate way to counteract drug interactions. Please understand that any adverse reaction from this combination needs professional medical assessment, not an adjustment to your prescription. For temporary relief, it is best to call a nurse advice line or urgent care clinic for guidance.",
      "source": "target",
